#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a73fe140-3a26-5c33-b76d-7182da90c8b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357312} {:answer/id #uuid "979248b0-67ce-5295-b739-98d0f9c9a5dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a73fe140-3a26-5c33-b76d-7182da90c8b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357312} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b698320-f962-5b20-9e94-4e9c1faef10c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121555} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8caaea8-b523-5b0a-9fd8-80d04d8092a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2+3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8caaea8-b523-5b0a-9fd8-80d04d8092a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2+3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357315} :answer-field/id #uuid "32b8cb01-fc5b-5716-b4d2-434fa63588ac" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121556} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9daa492b-2b2f-5a2a-870c-36a8804a3e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9daa492b-2b2f-5a2a-870c-36a8804a3e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357314} :answer-field/id #uuid "7130e2d3-e72f-5f58-9976-df3b576f08aa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9a10a92-511c-5609-8370-301fff1b284f" :question/math-academy-id "q-236389" :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(-2,3,1).$\n\n| $x=$ | {{field-1}} | $t\\in [0,$ {{field-2}} $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $4-t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3t \\\\ -t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+3t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-3t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a3199e0-7ca6-5317-9afa-2d99c3b3771e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a3199e0-7ca6-5317-9afa-2d99c3b3771e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357316} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d7476b-5763-583f-adf2-eca36812c205" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121558} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58069a6a-b603-54fd-bc70-e51cd1dd4dd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58069a6a-b603-54fd-bc70-e51cd1dd4dd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357317} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed0572da-5a04-5fb8-88a9-093250d4d10a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121559}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca21829b-f75e-5a9d-97e2-6ce18378c4e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-236986" :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(-5,7,1)$ and $Q(-4,-1,6).$\n\n| $x=$ | {{field-1}} | $t\\in [$ {{field-2}} $,1]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $7-8t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | $1+5t$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ -8t \\\\ 5t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5+t \\\\ 7-8t \\\\ 1+5t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-5+t \\\\ y=7-8t \\\\ z=1+5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51ccc64f-ba35-50df-9939-e2a12ff85188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-5+3t \\\\ y=-11+6t \\\\ z=-4+8t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357320} {:answer/id #uuid "84f3e9f8-8af0-5a19-b3fe-fc9c0ea0f5f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=3t \\\\ y=6t \\\\ z=8t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357321} {:answer/id #uuid "8f95886e-0710-5d17-9e90-55fc7b4dee02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=6-11t \\\\ z=8-4t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357322} {:answer/id #uuid "fc9d07b8-653d-5448-9865-94f13110407e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2+3t \\\\ y=-5+6t \\\\ z=4+8t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357323} {:answer/id #uuid "5414db53-6619-56bb-8449-68daf5d5bc2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-5t \\\\ y=-11t \\\\ z=-4t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f95886e-0710-5d17-9e90-55fc7b4dee02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=6-11t \\\\ z=8-4t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357322} :answer-field/id #uuid "4140aab5-f5b9-5b71-bde7-b995e7150c80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e0ace14-c4d0-53ea-821e-4f626073eb45" :question/math-academy-id "q-32818" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/assets/99504eaa41497c5be9baa7c860c97ab5ba5c858609e47ad347f24ec9b8ffc940.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure above." :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(3,6,8)$ and $Q(-2,-5,4).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5t \\\\ -11t \\\\ -4t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3-5t \\\\ 6-11t \\\\ 8-4t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the parametric equations are:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=6-11t \\\\ z=8-4t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b80a7c1-1043-53df-9937-1c302aea271a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357326} {:answer/id #uuid "c7131830-fa04-52c9-8165-83976213e7df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4+t \\\\ y=-1+4t \\\\ z=2-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357327} {:answer/id #uuid "26149efd-6258-5c6d-899b-8b76bd92f6a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=4t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357328} {:answer/id #uuid "a1bd0392-0d4d-5e20-af94-0f8eea17c8ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=5+t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357329} {:answer/id #uuid "31cb1ef6-a234-5bb7-b23d-06c409656e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=-t \\\\ z=2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b80a7c1-1043-53df-9937-1c302aea271a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357326} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9a7ef8f-c4b6-5c5b-9714-eade580df09e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3a37d06-4a0c-5126-bd3b-fbb999a13c7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-36026" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1+4t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37269206-ff38-5158-a69f-5bf7c914f100" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357333} {:answer/id #uuid "f82d71d4-c76a-5493-8fe9-fe5cdb5c703c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357334} {:answer/id #uuid "b1599866-bc5c-5705-82d6-f8df38ef492f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357335} {:answer/id #uuid "43563c92-436c-5119-9cdc-0d2a1ad58c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357336} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e16bed-11d8-56fc-9786-9b35848e825a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37269206-ff38-5158-a69f-5bf7c914f100" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357333} :answer-field/id #uuid "970e7078-7224-55a4-b236-058de0e89bbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b555bc5f-ed8b-573d-be10-fd205e56f99f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70722" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{1}{2}t+1 \\\\ y=5-\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ z=2t+\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}t+1 \\\\ 5-\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ 2t+\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(1,5,\\frac{1}{3})$  and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$"}]}
